4. Integrated random interacting multiple model filtering
When the model set is completely correct, IMM performs well. However, when the model set can not cover the target state, the IMM errors diverge and become large. Back to our random motion model, it performs stably but the accuracy is a little worse than IMM with right models. In this section, we will propose a novel algorithm combine the advantages of random motion model and IMM, called integrated random interacting multiple models (IRIMM). The main idea of the new algorithm is to use the IMM algorithm to calculate the model probabilities at first, and then use RKF to estimate the target state. Compared with IMM, IRIMM has two differences: 1) The random model is introduced into the algorithm model set, and the model set includes both deterministic models and random motion model; 2) In state estimation, the estimation of IMM is acquired by a weighted average method. The basic idea of IRIMM is to integrate all models and measurements to a new whole system. Then the random coefficient matrices Kalman filtering is applied to this integrated dynamic system to derive the estimate of the target state.
